From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hans2294 <22217531+hans2294@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:55:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Haiku support on linuxkpi

DRM nodes on Haiku are linuxkpi devices: their Linux dev_t and PCI
device come from LINUXKPI_IOCTL_DEVICE_INFO (stat()/fstat() wrappers fill
st_rdev, and the subsystem and PCI parsers ask the node), the sibling
node of a device is found by its PCI address, and buffers are mapped with
LINUXKPI_IOCTL_MMAP/MUNMAP instead of mmap().

haiku/ holds the build pieces Haiku's Jam build uses: config.h (with
positive POSIX errors), Linux's ioctl encoding as sys/ioccom.h, and the
generated format modifier table.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
